{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_030","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"cd ComfyUI\npip install -r requirements.txt","location_hint":"paragraph 119","char_start":3941,"char_end":3983,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_031","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"Use the command line to enter the installation path of ComfyUI, then pull the latest code.","location_hint":"paragraph 128","char_start":4124,"char_end":4214,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_032","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"cd < installation pat h > /ComfyUI\ngit pull","location_hint":"paragraph 129","char_start":4218,"char_end":4261,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_033","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"Use the command line to enter the installation path of ComfyUI, then install the dependencies.","location_hint":"paragraph 132","char_start":4299,"char_end":4393,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_034","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"You need to ensure that the current Python environment is the ComfyUI virtual environment, otherwise the dependencies will be installed to the system-level Python environment, polluting the system-level Python environment.","location_hint":"paragraph 133","char_start":4397,"char_end":4619,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_035","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"pip install -r requirements.txt","location_hint":"paragraph 134","char_start":4623,"char_end":4654,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_036","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"If you want to manage your model files outside of ComfyUI/models , you may have the following reasons:","location_hint":"paragraph 137","char_start":4690,"char_end":4792,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_037","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"You have multiple ComfyUI instances and want them to share model files to save disk space","location_hint":"paragraph 138","char_start":4795,"char_end":4884,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_038","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"You have different types of GUI programs (such as WebUI) and want them to use the same model files","location_hint":"paragraph 139","char_start":4886,"char_end":4984,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_039","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"Model files cannot be recognized or found","location_hint":"paragraph 140","char_start":4986,"char_end":5027,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_040","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"We provide a way to add extra model search paths via the extra_model_paths.yaml configuration file","location_hint":"paragraph 141","char_start":5030,"char_end":5128,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_041","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"For the ComfyUI version such as portable and manual , you can find an example file named extra_model_paths.yaml.example in the root directory of ComfyUI:","location_hint":"paragraph 146","char_start":5201,"char_end":5354,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_042","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"ComfyUI/extra_model_paths.yaml.example","location_hint":"paragraph 147","char_start":5358,"char_end":5396,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_043","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"Copy and rename it to extra_model_paths.yaml for use. Keep it in ComfyUI’s root directory at ComfyUI/extra_model_paths.yaml .\nYou can also find the config example file here","location_hint":"paragraph 148","char_start":5399,"char_end":5571,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_044","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"If you are using the ComfyUI Desktop application, you can follow the image below to open the extra model config file: Or open it directly at:","location_hint":"paragraph 149","char_start":5573,"char_end":5714,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_045","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"C:\\Users\\YourUsername\\AppData\\Roaming\\ComfyUI\\extra_models_config.yaml","location_hint":"paragraph 152","char_start":5738,"char_end":5808,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_046","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"~/Library/Application Support/ComfyUI/extra_models_config.yaml","location_hint":"paragraph 153","char_start":5813,"char_end":5875,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_047","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"You should keep the file in the same directory, should not move these files to other places.","location_hint":"paragraph 154","char_start":5878,"char_end":5970,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_048","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"If the file does not exist, you can create it yourself with any text editor.","location_hint":"paragraph 155","char_start":5972,"char_end":6048,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_049","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"Suppose you want to add the following model paths to ComfyUI:","location_hint":"paragraph 158","char_start":6076,"char_end":6137,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_664a4a54b4c3_050","source_id":"src_664a4a54b4c3","source_hash":"c62e4571c3aeadb02f462f4f969b614956dc4d142c956e43ec12a7fcb6967a34","text":"📁 YOUR_PATH/\n├── 📁models/\n| ├── 📁 loras/\n| │ └── xxxxx.safetensors\n| ├── 📁 checkpoints/\n| │ └── xxxxx.safetensors\n| ├── 📁 vae/\n| │ └── xxxxx.safetensors\n| └── 📁 controlnet/\n| └── xxxxx.safetensors","location_hint":"paragraph 159","char_start":6141,"char_end":6343,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.667Z"}
